## 2. `include/strata/artifact/gguf_split.hpp` — `gguf_split_paths` accepts non-digit shard digits inconsistently

**Responsibilities.** Resolve any shard path of a split model to the ordered shard list, erroring on a missing shard.

**Change.** The digit loop returns `{any}` (treat as single file) when a digit is bad, but `at < 6` and the `any[at-6] != '-'` checks return `{any}` too — a path like `model-00001-of-00002.ggu` (wrong extension length) falls through `any.size() != at + 4 + 5 + 5` and is silently treated as one file, so a truncated download of a *renamed* shard is not detected. Tighten: when the `-of-` tag exists and the shape is *almost* right (correct length, bad digits), throw rather than silently returning one path, because that is exactly the "download still running / renamed file" case the header comment says must be an error.

```diff
--- a/include/strata/artifact/gguf_split.hpp
+++ b/include/strata/artifact/gguf_split.hpp
@@
     int no = 0, n = 0;
     for (size_t i = 0; i < 5; ++i) {
         const char a = any[at - 5 + i], b = any[at + 4 + i];
-        if (a < '0' || a > '9' || b < '0' || b > '9') return {any};
+        if (a < '0' || a > '9' || b < '0' || b > '9')
+            throw std::runtime_error("model shard name '" + any +
+                                     "' has the -NNNNN-of-MMMMM shape but a non-digit shard number");
         no = no * 10 + (a - '0');
         n = n * 10 + (b - '0');
     }
-    if (n < 1 || no < 1 || no > n) return {any};
+    if (n < 1 || no < 1 || no > n)
+        throw std::runtime_error("model shard name '" + any + "' declares shard " + std::to_string(no) +
+                                 " of " + std::to_string(n));
```

**Verification.**
1. `gguf_split_test`: existing cases (valid 4-shard family, single file, missing shard names the file) still pass.
2. New cases: `foo-0000x-of-00004.gguf` and `foo-00005-of-00004.gguf` now throw with the name in the message; `foo.gguf` and `foo-of-1.gguf` (wrong digit count) still return `{any}`.

