## 4. `include/strata/core/conversation_buffer.hpp` — `resize` shrink path can underflow on a zero-size segment

**Responsibilities.** Snapshot-owned segmented host storage; append never relocates payloads.

**Change.** In the shrink branch, `while (!segments_.empty() && size_ - segments_.back().size() >= n)` assumes `segments_.back().size() <= size_`. A `resize(0)` followed by `resize(k)` then `resize(0)` is fine, but a hand-built buffer (or a future `reserve`-style API) with an empty trailing segment makes `size_ - 0 >= n` loop forever only if `n < size_`… actually it pops correctly. The real hazard: `segments_.back().resize(segments_.back().size() - (size_ - n))` when `size_ - n > back().size()` (possible if the while loop exited because `size_ - back().size() < n` while `size_ > n`) underflows `size_t`. Add the guard:

```diff
--- a/include/strata/core/conversation_buffer.hpp
+++ b/include/strata/core/conversation_buffer.hpp
@@
             while (!segments_.empty() && size_ - segments_.back().size() >= n) {
                 size_ -= segments_.back().size();
                 segments_.pop_back();
             }
-            if (size_ > n) segments_.back().resize(segments_.back().size() - (size_ - n));
+            if (size_ > n) {
+                const size_t drop = size_ - n;
+                if (drop > segments_.back().size()) return;   // invariant: cannot happen; refuse rather than underflow
+                segments_.back().resize(segments_.back().size() - drop);
+            }
             size_ = n;
```

**Verification.**
1. Existing conversation snapshot tests (`conversation_snapshot_test`, `conversation_validation_test`) pass unchanged.
2. A new case in `conv_cache_test`-style CPU test: build a buffer, `resize(10)`, `resize(3)`, `resize(7)`, `resize(0)`; assert `size()==0`, `empty()`, and that a fuzz loop of random resize sequences never crashes and always satisfies `read()` equality against a `std::vector` reference.

