## 5. `include/strata/core/conversation_cache.hpp` — `retain()` can underflow when `bytes_ > budget_`

**Responsibilities.** Ownership and matching policy for parked conversations.

**Change.** `if (enabled() && candidate.bytes() <= budget_ - bytes_)` underflows when `bytes_ > budget_` (possible after `limit_reuse`/eviction races are extended). Use the saturating form already used in `can_fit`:

```diff
--- a/include/strata/core/conversation_cache.hpp
+++ b/include/strata/core/conversation_cache.hpp
@@
     void retain(std::vector<ConversationKv>&& kv, int64_t tokens) {
         reuse_ = {};
         ConversationKvReuse candidate{std::move(kv), tokens, tokens};
-        if (enabled() && candidate.bytes() <= budget_ - bytes_) reuse_ = std::move(candidate);
+        if (enabled() && bytes_ <= budget_ && candidate.bytes() <= budget_ - bytes_) reuse_ = std::move(candidate);
     }
```

**Verification.**
1. `conversation_cache_test` passes; the existing "retain never evicts a parked conversation" scenario is unchanged.
2. New case: construct `ConversationCache(100, 4)`, `put` an image of 120 bytes (must fail), then `retain()` a 50-byte KV and assert `retained_bytes()==0` and no crash (before the fix this is `100 - 120` → huge).

---

## 6. `include/strata/core/coupled_draft.hpp` — `coupled_hist_base` ignores `h > cap`

**Responsibilities.** Counter arithmetic and penalty-ring geometry for coupled draft sampling.

**Change.** `coupled_hist_len` clamps to `cap`, but `coupled_hist_base` takes `h` from the caller; if a caller passes `h > kCoupledHistCap`, `penalty_rows` writes past `out`. Clamp inside the function (it is header-only and cheap):

```diff
--- a/include/strata/core/coupled_draft.hpp
+++ b/include/strata/core/coupled_draft.hpp
@@
 inline void coupled_hist_base(const int32_t* tail, int64_t n_tail, int32_t next, int h, int32_t* out) {
     if (h <= 0) return;
-    strata::kernels::penalty_rows(tail, n_tail, &next, 1, h, out);
+    strata::kernels::penalty_rows(tail, n_tail, &next, 1, coupled_hist_len(h, kCoupledHistCap), out);
 }
```

**Verification.**
1. `coupled_draft_test` passes; the ring-window identities (`coupled_hist_start` + `h` == `cap + j`) are unchanged for legal `h`.
2. New case: `coupled_hist_base(tail, 5000, 7, 9000, out)` writes exactly `kCoupledHistCap` slots and the last slot equals `next`; ASan build of the test reports no overflow.

