## 7. `include/strata/core/device.hpp` / `src/core/device.cu` — `DeviceArena::alloc` does not check alignment is a power of two

**Responsibilities.** One-cudaMalloc bump arena.

**Change.** The header documents "`align` must be a power of two" but nothing enforces it; a caller passing 200 silently mis-rounds. Add a debug assert and a safe fallback:

```diff
--- a/include/strata/core/device.hpp
+++ b/include/strata/core/device.hpp
@@
     // `align` must be a power of two; 256 keeps every sub-allocation at a sector boundary.
     void* alloc(uint64_t bytes, uint64_t align = 256);
+    // (implementation) rounds align DOWN to the next power of two and reports it once, rather than
+    // producing an unaligned pointer that a vectorized kernel then faults on.
```

and in `src/core/device.cu`:

```diff
--- a/src/core/device.cu
+++ b/src/core/device.cu
@@
 void* DeviceArena::alloc(uint64_t bytes, uint64_t align) {
+    if (align == 0 || (align & (align - 1)) != 0) {
+        uint64_t p = 1;
+        while (p < align) p <<= 1;
+        std::fprintf(stderr, "strata: DeviceArena::align %llu is not a power of two; using %llu\n",
+                     (unsigned long long) align, (unsigned long long) p);
+        align = p;
+    }
     const uint64_t a = (used_ + align - 1) / align * align;
```

**Verification.**
1. `platform_memory_test` and `strata-device --selftest` unchanged.
2. New case: `alloc(100, 200)` returns a pointer aligned to 256 and prints the warning once; `alloc(100, 0)` does not divide by zero.

---

## 8. `include/strata/core/expert_cache.hpp` — `admit()` per-layer range can hand out slot 0 twice when `slots_ < n_layers_`

**Responsibilities.** VRAM expert slot storage and residency table.

**Change.** `layer_slot_range` with `q = slots_/n_layers_` gives `q == 0` when the cache is smaller than the layer count; every layer's range is then `[l*0, (l+1)*0)` = empty except the last layer's remainder, so `admit` either refuses everything or (depending on the remainder branch) two layers share a slot. Refuse per-layer admission at `open` time when it cannot be honoured:

```diff
--- a/include/strata/core/expert_cache.hpp
+++ b/include/strata/core/expert_cache.hpp
@@
     void set_per_layer_admission(bool on) { per_layer_ = on; }
+    /// Whether the slot count can honour per-layer admission (>= n_layers slots).  The driver must
+    /// check this before enabling it; with fewer slots than layers the ranges collapse and two layers
+    /// would share one slot.
+    bool per_layer_admissible() const { return slots_ >= n_layers_; }
```

and in `ExpertCache::admit` (src/core/expert_cache.cpp) add at the top of the per-layer branch:

```diff
-    if (per_layer_) { ... }
+    if (per_layer_) {
+        if (slots_ < n_layers_) return kNotResident;   // ranges would overlap; refuse rather than alias
+        ...
+    }
```

**Verification.**
1. `
